# D0_3 (Fe3Al-type) ordering target on BCC 4x4x4 = 128 atoms.
# Species: 0 = A (Fe-like, 75%), 1 = B (Al-like, 25%).
#
# D0_3 has a 16-atom cubic cell = 2x2x2 BCC; ours holds 8 such cells.
# Sublattice population: A on 4a + 8c (= 12 of 16), B on 4b (= 4 of 16).
#
# Warren-Cowley signature averaged over the 75:25 sublattice:
#   shell 0 (NN, z=8): every Al has 8 Fe NN; aggregate P(Al|Fe) = 1/3
#                      -> alpha_AB = 1 - (1/3)/0.25 = -1/3 (max ordering)
#   shell 1 (2NN, z=6): Fe_4a has 6 Al, Fe_8c has 0 Al; aggregate
#                      P(Al|Fe) = 1/3 -> alpha_AB = -1/3 (also max ordering)
#
# Both shells maximally ordered (-1/3 each) is the D0_3 signature on
# 75:25 BCC; saturates the bound at both NN and 2NN simultaneously.
SRO 0 1 0 -0.333333
SRO 0 1 1 -0.333333
